  "body": "First slice of #1446: the rest-machining generator in the motion crate. The operation parameter, its undoable edit, the project file, the dialog group and the MCP parameters are not in this PR (follow-ups below), so nothing a user can reach changes yet and no posted G-code changes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest2d.rs` (new):\n  - `rest_plan(region, tool_diameter, stock_to_leave, &RestParams) -> RestPlan`: the rest area (what a larger previous tool could not reach) and the cutter-center area that touches it.\n  - `rest_pocket(region, &PocketParams, &RestParams) -> Toolpath`: the pocket's ring passes over that area only.\n  - `RestParams`: previous tool diameter, previous tool corner radius, stock the previous operation left on the walls, rest allowance. The previous tool is entered, and the path says in a note that it is trusted.\n- `pocket.rs`: the body of `pocket()` is now `pocket_over(region, center, p, notes, hold_crossings)`, shared with the rest pass. `pocket()` computes its center area and calls it with no notes and the switch off: the plain pocket posts as before. `PocketStrategy` moved to `pocket_strategy.rs` (structure only; `pocket.rs` 456 -> 427 lines, still over the 400-line law it was already over).\n- `docs/decisions/1446-rest-2d.md`: the decisions taken.\n\n## How the rest area is read\n\nRest = pocket minus the opening of the pocket by the previous tool's disc (inward offset by its radius, then outward). It is read large, never small:\n\n- the cleared area is shrunk by 0.01 mm (`REST_MARGIN`, two offset arc tolerances) before it is subtracted;\n- a previous tool with a corner radius sweeps only its flat; stock left on the walls is rest material; the allowance only grows the area (negative is refused);\n- the one reduction is a film thinner than 0.02 mm (`REST_FILM`), without which every wall would read as rest material;\n- the cutter-center area is the rest area grown by the tool radius plus 0.05 mm (`REST_REACH`), cut to the plain pocket's own center area: a rest pass cannot touch a wall the plain pocket would not.\n\nNo rapid relies on the estimate: below the top of the cut every move is a plunge or a feed, and separate rest areas are linked by a retract. A wrong previous tool costs a heavier cut, not a rapid into stock.\n\nRefused by name: a previous tool that is not larger than this tool; non-finite or negative values; a corner radius larger than the tool radius; `Zigzag` (its rows left residue in the corner in the coverage test); `Adaptive` (not built for rest areas); nothing left to cut (`GenError::Empty`, \"no rest material\"); a pocket narrower than the tool. `Auto` reads as `Waterline` for a rest pass. A previous tool that fits nowhere leaves the whole pocket: the path equals the plain pocket's, with a note.\n\nTwo things found while testing, both recorded in the decisions file: fitted arcs crossed each other at the thin horns of a rest area (verifier Crossing law, neck fixture), so the rest rings go through the existing `arc_cross` proof as the Adaptive plan does; and the bare-radius reach left slivers along the pocket's own center boundary, hence `REST_REACH`.\n\n## Readings (fixture: 60 x 40 pocket, 3 mm corners, previous tool 12 mm, this tool 4 mm)\n\n- Rest area: 4 loops, one per corner, each inside its 6 mm corner box; area within -0.05 / +1.5 mm2 of the exact 23.18 mm2; 0 of more than 1500 grid points of certain residue missing; 0 grid points of rest area deeper than 0.2 mm into cleared floor.\n- Rest passes (Waterline, Offset rings, Auto): verifier (`Mode::Area`) clean; every cutting move within 8.3 mm of a corner; the only rapids below the top of the cut are straight lifts; every certain-residue grid point is under the tool at the floor; cutting length at the floor under 25 % of the full pocket's.\n- Neck fixture (two bays joined by a 6 mm neck): the neck is rest material and is cut through; 9 center areas, none a sliver; verifier clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs` (10 tests): `rest_area_is_the_four_corners_and_never_reads_small`, `rest_passes_cut_only_the_corners_and_cover_them`, `rest_pass_is_far_shorter_than_the_full_pocket`, `previous_tool_not_larger_is_refused_by_name`, `bad_rest_parameters_are_refused_by_name`, `nothing_left_is_refused_not_cut`, `previous_tool_that_fits_nowhere_leaves_the_whole_pocket`, `a_neck_the_previous_tool_could_not_pass_is_rest_material`, `allowance_stock_and_corner_radius_only_grow_the_rest_area`, `degenerate_pockets_error_and_never_panic`.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green on the head (motion suites 242 s, app suites 463 s, 0 failed); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The toolpaths were not run on a machine.\n- No stock simulation: \"no pass over cleared floor\" and \"no plunge into uncut stock\" are read from the path geometry and the verifier, not from a simulated roughing pass followed by the rest pass.\n- No golden CL (the golden helpers live in the app tests; the motion tests pin readings) and nothing through the app, the UI, the project file or MCP: none of it is wired.\n- The previous tool is entered and trusted. A roughing pass that did not reach the stated depth, or used another tool, is not detected.\n- Adaptive and Zigzag with rest are refused, not built. Pockets with islands and stock to leave on this operation are covered by the construction but have no fixture of their own.\n- Windows only; debug build.\n\n## Literature\n\n- J. Serra, \"Image Analysis and Mathematical Morphology\", Academic Press, 1982 (erosion, dilation, opening).\n- M. Held, \"On the Computational Geometry of Pocket Machining\", LNCS 500, Springer, 1991 (offsets and the machinable area).\n- D. Veeramani, Y.-S. Gau, \"Selection of an optimal set of cutting-tool sizes for 2.5D pocket machining\", Computer-Aided Design 29(12), 1997.\n- Z. Yao, S. K. Gupta, D. S. Nau, \"Algorithms for selecting cutters in multi-part milling problems\", Computer-Aided Design 35(9), 2003.\n\nThe citations were found by a literature search and checked by title and venue; the papers' full texts were not read line by line, and the construction used is the textbook opening they share. No code or text from stevecad/camlib or any other CAM product was read or used; no HSMWorks material.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- #1489: the Pocket operation parameter (default off), its undoable edit, the project file, the dialog group, the MCP parameters, the golden CL through the app and the stock-simulation reading.\n- #1490: Adaptive over a rest area, entry from already-cut space, the previous tool read from the carried stock, Zigzag.\n\nNo UI change, so no screenshots.\n\nChangelog: 2D rest machining generator in the motion crate: the rest area a larger previous tool left and the ring passes that cut only it; not wired to an operation yet\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1446\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
